    <string name="about_title">About SealRec</string>
    <string name="about_proves_title">What SealRec proves</string>
    <string name="about_proves_body">The PCM hash matches a signature verified with the embedded key. This does not identify a person or device. Audio format and timestamps are not signed. Repaired recordings are sealed at recovery time. WAV files are not encrypted.</string>
    <string name="about_not_title">What it does NOT prove</string>
    <string name="about_not_body">SealRec cannot prove who was speaking, where the recording happened, or that the sounds themselves were not staged or replayed from a speaker. It only proves the digital file has not been altered since it was sealed.</string>
    <string name="about_time_title">About DeviceTime</string>
    <string name="about_time_body">The timestamp embedded in each seal comes from the device\'s local clock, not a trusted timestamping authority (TSA). If the system clock was wrong or changed, the sealed time will reflect that. Treat it as a hint, not as proof of when the recording was made.</string>
